From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:40:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] drm/imagination: Restore evicted VM mappings before
 arming jobs

A faultless GPU must never start work with a hole left by reclaim.
The first render on the iPad 5 hung before firmware boot when the HWRT
dependency walk reacquired a reservation already owned by drm_exec.
Assert ownership there instead of taking a NULL-ticket recursive lock.
Lock each distinct submission VM before taking any reservation, validate
the GPUVM evict list, and retain VM locks through arming, VM fence
publication and queueing. Serialize submissions with the existing order
mutex, now common, as the nesting anchor for multiple VM locks. Map and
unmap only take one VM lock, then reservations; reclaim only trylocks.

PowerVR uses GPUVM flags zero and does not populate its extobj list.
Keep the internally spinlocked evict list, add vm_bo_validate, and use
drm_gpuvm_prepare_range over the actual VA tree in the drm_exec retry
pass. Restore every marked VA from its new DMA-mapped sgt, publish the
flush, clear eviction and refresh LRU recency. Keep prior restores on a
failure and return -ENOMEM before prepare_job_syncs can arm anything.

Track eviction per VA for mixed resident/evicted mappings and splits.
Unmap skips cleared PTEs. Repair a partial eviction by clearing its full
range before remapping. Move VM_MAP's page acquisition and MMU cursor
creation under the VM and BO locks: a bare sgt obtained before either
lock could otherwise be freed by reclaim before MAP uses it.

Native validation defers context and HWRT reservations until its MMU
flush completes: the flush error path resets and vmaps firmware objects.
Reinitialize exec for the full reservation pass before dependencies; VM
mutexes keep residency protected across both passes. Apple uses its
RAM-only invalidation with the complete reservation set held.

Affects: every PowerVR device

Assisted-by: LLM
